WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.700
April 15, 2013 – two bombs tear through
the crowd welcoming runners over the finish

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.379
line at the Boston Marathon.

00:00:07.379 --> 00:00:11.610
The carnage is total with three people killed
and dozens wounded.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:14.310
Within hours the FBI have identified a pair
of suspects.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:18.420
The two brothers are immigrants to America
whose parents have fled the violence of Chechnya

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:20.540
to give their children a better life.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.880
So, how did it all go so wrong?

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:27.869
Today, through the story of the younger of
the two bombers, Dzokhar Tsarnaev, we find

00:00:27.869 --> 00:00:31.230
out.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:37.949
Early Years

00:00:37.949 --> 00:00:46.079
Dzhokhar Anzorovich Tsarnaev was born on July
22, 1993 in Kyrgyzstan.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:49.079
His parents were Anzor and Zubeidat Tsarnaev.

00:00:49.079 --> 00:00:53.070
Anzor was a cattle farm laborer in the Caspian
region of Kalmykia.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:57.690
Zubeidat was a city girl who struggled to
fit into the rural community life that marriage

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.690
gave her.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:01.999
Her spirits were lifted with the birth of
her first child in October, 1986.

00:01:01.999 --> 00:01:06.210
The couple named the boy Tamerlan, after the
great Asian conqueror.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.780
Zubeidat was a doting mother.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:11.200
She always dressed Tamerlane, who was nicknamed
Tami, in the best attire.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:12.750
The boy did well in school.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:16.460
His mother put pressure on her husband to
move in order to provide their son with wider

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:17.460
opportunities.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.500
They returned to Anzor’s hometown of Anzor
and moved in with his parents.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:23.799
About a year later, Anzor’s father was killed
in a work accident.

00:01:23.799 --> 00:01:25.890
This left him as the family patriarch.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:30.180
With the collapse of the Soviet Union, life
in the region changed dramatically.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:33.690
Laborers became entrepreneurs overnight as
the western economy began flooding in.

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:36.299
Anzor found a job as a car repairman.

00:01:36.299 --> 00:01:40.219
He was making a living but in order to really
get ahead he realized that he had to get to

00:01:40.219 --> 00:01:45.100
the newly created republic of Chechnya, which
seemed like the new promised land.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:49.690
The family, which now included two daughters,
moved to Chechnya in 1992.

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:52.280
It was there that their second son, Dzhokhar
was born.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:56.509
He was named after the charismatic new President
of Chechnya, Dzhokhar Dudayev.

00:01:56.509 --> 00:01:59.079
Within a year, things had gone horribly wrong.

00:01:59.079 --> 00:02:03.119
The Russians invaded Chechnya and the Tsarnaev’s
found themselves in the middle of a war zone.

00:02:03.119 --> 00:02:08.250
The family piled into a battered old Skoda
and drove back to Kyrgyzstan and the old family

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:09.590
home in Tokmok.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:14.270
They settled back into their old lives, while
also making plans to get out of Eastern Europe.

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:16.650
Their goal was America.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:20.210
Anzor and Zubeidat believed that their chances
of getting to America would be improved if

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:22.370
they obtained some educational credentials.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:25.900
As a result, they both began studying law
part time.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:31.210
After four years in Tokmok they sold the family
home and moved, not to America, but to Zubeidat’s

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:32.250
hometown of Dagestan.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:37.420
However, it seemed as if this family was unable
to escape from war, and before long the streets

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:41.450
there were filled with gunfights and explosions.

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:47.930
Coming to America
The Tsarnaev family moved once again.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:51.170
Anzor and Zubeidat took Dzhokhar with them
on a trip to the United States.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:55.630
Tamerlan, along with the two daughters, was
left with their uncle in Kyrgyzstan.

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:57.480
They traveled on a 90-day tourist visa.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:01.690
During that visit, Anzor applied for political
asylum, claiming that his life was in danger

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:03.990
due to his connections with Chechnya.

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:07.650
The application was submitted and the family
were allowed to stay until a decision was

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:08.650
reached.

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:11.350
The Tsarnaev’s had chosen to come to Boston,
Massachusetts.

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:14.710
That was where some friends had moved the
previous year, so at least they would know

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:15.710
somebody.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:19.300
They moved in with this couple and the eight-year-old
Dzhokhar began attending second grade at a

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.650
public school along with two of the Biev children.

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:27.120
In April 2002, Anzor managed to find an inexpensive
apartment in Cambridge, Massachusetts and

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.280
they moved out of the Biev home and into their
own place.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:34.020
Dzhokhar was left with the Biev’s for the
meantime in order not to interrupt his school

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:35.020
year.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:38.680
Anzor and Zubeidat presented themselves as
prospective lawyers, even though their studies

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:39.730
had been minimal.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:42.890
The were, they told people, fleeing from ethnic
strife.

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:47.440
They found a kindred spirit in their landlord,
Joanna Herlihy, who took them under her wing.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:52.210
She took Zubeidat to an Amnesty International
event focused on human rights abuses in Chechnya

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:56.170
and even paid for her to enroll in a Harvard
extension course on negotiation.

00:03:56.170 --> 00:04:00.410
Anzor picked up under the table jobs fixing
cars for ten dollars an hour.

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:03.910
When the school year was over, Dzhokhar came
to live with his parents in Cambridge.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:05.730
His time with the Biev’s had been challenging.

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:09.900
The parents insisted that the only language
spoken in the home was Chechen, which he could

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:11.380
barely understand.

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:13.830
When the parents weren’t around, the children
would speak Russian.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:17.930
He learned English from his association with
American kids at school, picking it up at

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:18.930
an amazing pace.

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:22.680
Dzhokhar soon became an accepted member of
the Chechen community of children in the local

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:23.680
area.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:25.070
He was a good student who made quick advancement.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:29.450
In fact, during his second year at school
he was bumped up from 3rd to 4th grade.

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:33.280
In mid-2003, the Tsarnaev’s asylum application
was granted.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:37.440
The three children left in Kyrgyzstan were
now free to join their family in the promised

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:38.440
land.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:41.340
With the family reunited, things were looking
pretty good for the immigrant family.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:47.140
Both Anzor and Zubeidat were working and they
had permanent, affordable accommodation.

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:55.270
Strange New Land
Dzhokhar is remembered as a sweet, lovable

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:56.270
boy.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:57.510
He was described as being charming.

00:04:57.510 --> 00:05:01.750
His teachers described him as being bright,
but lacking in the ability to think creatively

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:02.760
for himself.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:05.470
He tended to say things that got other people
to like him.

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:07.870
In 2003, Dzhokhar entered fifth grade.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:11.860
His sisters, thirteen-year-old Ailina and
fifteen-year-old Bella were in seventh and

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:15.750
ninth grades, while seventeen-year-old Tamerlan
was in tenth grade.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:20.240
The landlady, Joanna, tutored the children
in English, took them to movies and lent them

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:21.320
DVDs to watch.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.960
Tamerlan, augmented his studies with Joanna
by reading Sherlock Holmes stories.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:29.030
Being the oldest son, Tamerlan was the focus
of the family’s plans for success.

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:32.550
He was the golden-haired child, the one who
was destined for greatness.

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:34.920
He was tall, muscular and handsome.

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:43.590
Even Americans saw something special in him.

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:45.050
The Older Brother
Anzor decided that, before heading off to

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:48.110
college, his oldest son would become a champion
boxer.

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:50.490
Tamerlan proved himself to be a gifted fighter.

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:55.360
He had a very unconventional stance, with
his arms hanging down rather than in a defensive

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:56.360
stance.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:06:00.080
After training with his father for a while,
he turned up at a local martial arts gym.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:04.410
He had no mouthpiece, helmet or other protective
gear, and claimed that he didn’t need them.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:06.530
When he got in the ring, he proved it.

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:10.889
His stated ambition was to win a spot on the
US Olympic team and to use that position as

00:06:10.889 --> 00:06:13.620
a way of becoming a naturalized US citizen.

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:18.130
Tamerlan’s first victory in boxing competition
was achieved in January, 2004.

00:06:18.130 --> 00:06:21.380
It was a golden gloves amateur bout held in
Lowell, Massachusetts.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:24.590
In his post victory interview, he said . . .
I like the USA.

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:28.900
You have a chance to make a lot of money here
if you are willing to work.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:32.570
In 2006, Tamerlan was enrolled at Bunker Hill
Community College.

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:34.880
For two years he focused on his studies.

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:37.480
Then, in 2009, he returned to boxing.

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:40.770
Within a year he had made it onto the national
amateur boxing circuit.

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:45.310
In 2010, he won the Rocky Marciano Trophy
for winning the New England Golden Gloves

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:46.310
competition.

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:50.350
But because he wasn’t a US citizen, he was
ineligible to fight for a national title.

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:55.470
This was a severe blow to Tamerlan and it
caused him to give up on his boxing career.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:58.430
By that time, Tamerlan had also dropped out
of college.

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:01.410
His focus now was on becoming a music star.

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:06.360
He began dressing flamboyantly, with one person
describing his look as that of an Italian

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:07.360
gigolo.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:11.889
While American teenage boys may have mocked
his look, the girls were entranced and he

00:07:11.889 --> 00:07:13.840
had no shortage of female admirers.

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:20.130
In 2011, Tamerlan, the great hope of the Tsarnaev
family, was a failed boxer, a college dropout

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:21.220
and a father.

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:25.000
He was still living at home with his parents,
though his girlfriend and child did not.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:28.410
For money he delivered pizza part time, and
sold marijuana on the side.

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:32.290
It was not exactly the career path that his
parents had in mind.

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:37.310
Despite their initial efforts to integrate
into American society, by 2011 the Tsarnaevs

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:39.130
had given up on trying.

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:43.460
After struggling with the language, with the
culture and even with buying things on credit,

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:45.940
they reverted back to what they were comfortable
with.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:48.250
They decided to live as Chechens’ transplanted.

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:54.220
Their home had the typical Chechen look- oriental
rugs, a large plush sofa, and mirrored credenza

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:55.680
housing plates.

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:59.949
Things had not panned out as they had envisioned
– their neighbors viewed them with suspicion,

00:07:59.949 --> 00:08:01.490
if not with outright hostility.

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:05.670
Their son was dealing drugs, both their daughters
had by them entered into disastrous marriages

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:12.310
and Anzor was spending his days fixing old
cars in the street.

00:08:12.310 --> 00:08:18.190
Jahar
In mid-2011, Dzhokhar graduated from Rindge

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:23.010
college and moved to the university of Massachusetts
at Dartmouth, where he lived on campus.

00:08:23.010 --> 00:08:25.750
A couple of months later his parents filed
for divorce.

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:30.010
By now all of the rest of his family had become
disillusioned with their life in America.

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:31.060
But not Dzhokhar.

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:34.649
He continued to make good grades and establish
solid, positive friendships.

00:08:34.649 --> 00:08:37.089
He maintained his friendly, happy outlook.

00:08:37.089 --> 00:08:39.089
At college he joined the wrestling team.

00:08:39.089 --> 00:08:42.749
He impressed his coaches with his humility
and constant requests at what he could do

00:08:42.749 --> 00:08:43.819
to improve.

00:08:43.819 --> 00:08:48.339
It was a marked contrast to the American boys
on the team.

00:08:48.339 --> 00:08:51.189
Before long, he was captain of the wrestling
team.

00:08:51.189 --> 00:08:54.930
Just like his older brother, however, Dzhokhar
was both smoking and selling dope.

00:08:54.930 --> 00:09:00.370
Yet, his image of the pure, sweet teenage
boy was so complete, that no-one had any inkling

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:01.370
of it.

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:05.560
Dzhokhar developed a friendship with one of
the college’s most respected professors.

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:08.050
Larry Aronson was the college’s official
photographer.

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:12.760
Aronson adopted Dzhokhar as his poster child
for kids from war torn zones who were now

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:13.920
attending Rindge college.

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:18.279
He also helped the boy to come up with a more
American friendly version of his name, Jahar.

00:09:18.279 --> 00:09:22.300
Aronson was interested in engaging Dozkhar
in discussions about what was going on in

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:25.920
Chechnya, but the teenager had no desire to
talk about his old country.

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:29.250
Aaronson said . . .
Whenever I tried to talk to him about being

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:34.060
Chechen, it meant nothing to him.

00:09:34.060 --> 00:09:39.339
Radicalization
Meanwhile Jahar’s older brother, Tamerlan,

00:09:39.339 --> 00:09:41.140
was moving in the other direction.

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:44.139
In January, 2012 he flew to Dagestan.

00:09:44.139 --> 00:09:46.449
He went to his old hometown of Makhachkala.

00:09:46.449 --> 00:09:50.560
This was the capital of Dagestan and, over
the last ten years, it had transformed itself

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:51.779
into a modern city.

00:09:51.779 --> 00:09:55.760
Tamerlan quickly fit into the social scene,
spending his days mixing with fervent young

00:09:55.760 --> 00:10:00.029
men in their twenties and thirties who talked
about their religion, their aspirations and

00:10:00.029 --> 00:10:01.649
the injustices in the world.

00:10:01.649 --> 00:10:05.670
He met many of his relatives, a number of
who were involved in organized crime.

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:10.540
Tamerlan joined a group called Union of the
Just, which was allied to the Hizb ut-Tahrir,

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:13.179
one of the largest Islamic organizations in
the world.

00:10:13.179 --> 00:10:17.939
He told members of the group that American
was a racist country that was deeply divided,

00:10:17.939 --> 00:10:21.209
with corrupt police and a xenophobic foreign
policy.

00:10:21.209 --> 00:10:24.819
When asked to compare America with Russia,
Tamerlan is reported to have said . . .

00:10:24.819 --> 00:10:28.300
I refuse to choose between two kinds of fecal
matter.

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:29.639
Both taste like shit.

00:10:29.639 --> 00:10:34.449
In July 2012, Tamerlan told his associates
that he urgently needed to return to the United

00:10:34.449 --> 00:10:37.069
States because he had a problem with his documentation.

00:10:37.069 --> 00:10:41.259
He intimated that he had no desire to go and
would come back soon.

00:10:41.259 --> 00:10:45.740
Tamerlan returned to Cambridge to discover
that his father had himself returned to Dagestan

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:49.009
and had started a successful car repair business
with his brother.

00:10:49.009 --> 00:10:54.199
A couple of weeks later, Zubeidat also returned
to Dagestan, not to reunite with her ex-husband

00:10:54.199 --> 00:10:55.929
but to live with her family.

00:10:55.929 --> 00:10:58.269
To Tamerlan, Dagestan was now home.

00:10:58.269 --> 00:11:01.320
He would only stay in the US long enough to
get his passport.

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:04.560
Joanna Herlihy, the Tsarnaev’s landlord
had become increasingly concerned with the

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:06.529
radicalization of the family.

00:11:06.529 --> 00:11:10.679
After a heated encounter with Tamerlan in
which he vented about his hatred of America,

00:11:10.679 --> 00:11:15.360
she issued an eviction notice.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:21.139
Frustration
Back at College, Jahar got a new roommate.

00:11:21.139 --> 00:11:23.870
Andrew Dwinells ws a young American go-getter.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:28.610
The engineering major was going places and
his very presence highlighted to Jahar just

00:11:28.610 --> 00:11:30.410
how inadequate he really was.

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:35.129
The two never spoke and only exchanged messages
when one of them was locked out of the room.

00:11:35.129 --> 00:11:39.200
Jahar had a small and tight-knit group of
friends, all of them being eastern European.

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:43.130
There was also a steady flow of customers
to his dorm room to buy pot.

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:47.160
Within a few months, Jahar’s social circle
had widened slightly to include a couple of

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:48.160
Americans.

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:51.040
They congregated off campus at the apartment
of a couple of members of the group.

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:54.809
Once, Jahar disclosed to a couple of the group
members that he knew how to make a bomb.

00:11:54.809 --> 00:11:58.619
He also said there were parts of the Koran
that were worth fighting for with force.

00:11:58.619 --> 00:12:02.759
Still, he was not a Muslim extremist, though
those in his group who had met his brother

00:12:02.759 --> 00:12:05.350
considered Tamerlan to be one.

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:13.040
The Bombings
Patriot’s Day 2013 occurred on April 15

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:14.040
in 2013.

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:16.939
It is a public holiday in Massachusetts and
on that day in Boston the Boston marathon

00:12:16.939 --> 00:12:17.939
is run.

00:12:17.939 --> 00:12:21.939
Two hours after the end of the marathon, at
2:49 pm, as runners were streaming cross the

00:12:21.939 --> 00:12:25.199
finish line, two bombs exploded near the end
of the course.

00:12:25.199 --> 00:12:28.720
Three people were killed and 264 others were
wounded.

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:32.309
In the immediate aftermath of the bombing,
the police scanned the crowd in an attempt

00:12:32.309 --> 00:12:34.490
to identify anyone who looked out of place.

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:38.369
Their first target was a Saudi Arabian man
who had actually been wounded in the blasts.

00:12:38.369 --> 00:12:42.920
He was quickly cleared and then three other
Muslim men were looked at, but all dismissed.

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:47.570
On Thursday, April 18th, the Boston Post published
a photo on its front page along with a banner

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:50.699
that read . . .
Bag Men: Feds Seek These Two Pictured at Boston

00:12:50.699 --> 00:12:51.699
Marathon.

00:12:51.699 --> 00:12:54.389
The two men were Tamerlan and Jahar Tsarnaev.

00:12:54.389 --> 00:12:57.709
When Larry Arronson picked up the paper, he
thought that one of the men looked amazingly

00:12:57.709 --> 00:12:58.880
like Jahar.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:02.000
Then when students at the university saw the
picture, they didn’t think that it looked

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:05.000
like Jahar – they were convinced that it
WAS him.

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:08.199
Still, his friends couldn’t believe that
he had been involved in the bombing.

00:13:08.199 --> 00:13:10.759
He just didn’t seem capable.

00:13:10.759 --> 00:13:14.489
Rather than going to the police of the FBI,
his friends went to Jahar’s dorm.

00:13:14.489 --> 00:13:15.989
But the door was locked.

00:13:15.989 --> 00:13:19.489
Unable to locate Jahar, his friends went back
to their dorm and proceeded to play Xbox.

00:13:19.489 --> 00:13:22.839
A short time later, one of them received a
text from Jahar that read . . .

00:13:22.839 --> 00:13:25.899
If you want you can go to my room and take
what’s there.

00:13:25.899 --> 00:13:29.100
They returned to the room, used a spare key
to get in and began to search his side of

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:30.100
it.

00:13:30.100 --> 00:13:33.850
One of them found a black backpack that contained
a large metal cylinder and a half empty jar

00:13:33.850 --> 00:13:34.850
of Vaseline.

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:44.319
He turned to his friends and said,
I think he used these to make

00:13:44.319 --> 00:13:45.319
the bomb.

00:13:45.319 --> 00:13:46.339
Fugitives
The FBI had been focused on Jahar as early

00:13:46.339 --> 00:13:47.369
as Wednesday morning.

00:13:47.369 --> 00:13:50.369
They had been studying video of the aftermath
of the explosions.

00:13:50.369 --> 00:13:52.869
It was noticed that Jahar didn’t react to
the blasts.

00:13:52.869 --> 00:13:57.370
While everyone one else ran ducked and screamed,
he just kept right on walking.

00:13:57.370 --> 00:14:01.290
They also noticed Tamerlan walking alongside,
nd again showing no reaction.

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:04.259
But they had no idea who these two men were.

00:14:04.259 --> 00:14:07.360
The images were issued to the American public
with a warning that they were considered to

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:09.439
be armed and dangerous.

00:14:09.439 --> 00:14:12.949
In the hours following the bombing, local
media blamed the pair on every crime committed

00:14:12.949 --> 00:14:15.949
in the area, including the murder of an MIT
police officer.

00:14:15.949 --> 00:14:17.839
They got that last accusation right.

00:14:17.839 --> 00:14:21.110
The brothers killed officer Sean Collier in
order to steal his gun.

00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:24.360
They then committed a carjacking at a Cambridge
gas station.

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:28.110
They were driving a Mercedes SUV, but they
were unaware that it was fitted with a GPS

00:14:28.110 --> 00:14:29.110
device.

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:30.929
This allowed the police to track their every
movement.

00:14:30.929 --> 00:14:35.869
They seemed to be driving around aimlessly,
which they were, having no post bombing plan

00:14:35.869 --> 00:14:36.869
of action.

00:14:36.869 --> 00:14:40.259
In their possession the brothers had five
homemade explosive devices, a semiautomatic

00:14:40.259 --> 00:14:42.709
handgun, a machete and a hunting knife.

00:14:42.709 --> 00:14:46.299
End Game
The police caught up with the Tsarnaev brother

00:14:46.299 --> 00:14:49.179
in the early morning hours of April 19th.

00:14:49.179 --> 00:14:52.820
They closed in on the brothers in a quiet
suburban street in the suburb of Watertown

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:54.480
and began randomly firing.

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:56.880
One of the officers was seriously wounded
by friendly fire.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:01.329
The brothers were behind cover and, when ordered
to give up, Jahar threw the explosives devices

00:15:01.329 --> 00:15:02.569
towards the cops.

00:15:02.569 --> 00:15:04.379
They exploded harmlessly in the street.

00:15:04.379 --> 00:15:09.279
The final shootout was between Tamerlan and
a Watertown police officer named Jedd Pugliese.

00:15:09.279 --> 00:15:13.040
The officer scored several body hits while
Tamerlan failed to find his target.

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:16.209
When his ammunition ran out, he threw his
gun at Pugliese.

00:15:16.209 --> 00:15:17.589
He then ran for it.

00:15:17.589 --> 00:15:18.589
Pugliese and another officer ran after him.

00:15:18.589 --> 00:15:20.449
They soon got to him and dragged him to the
ground.

00:15:20.449 --> 00:15:24.549
But now Jahar jumped behind the wheel of the
SUV and proceeded to run down the officers.

00:15:24.549 --> 00:15:28.360
They officers quickly jumped aside, and Jahar
unwittingly drove over top of his brother,

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:30.660
dragging the body thirty feet down the street.

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:33.309
Leaving his brother dying on the road, Jahar
sped away.

00:15:33.309 --> 00:15:35.679
It took nearly a minute for the police to
give chase.

00:15:35.679 --> 00:15:38.149
By then, he’d ditched the car and run off
into the suburbs.

00:15:38.149 --> 00:15:41.139
A huge manhunt now swung into action, with
police officers scouring backyards in dozens

00:15:41.139 --> 00:15:44.329
of suburbs and thousands of people being ordered
to evacuate their homes.

00:15:44.329 --> 00:15:46.930
In the early afternoon of Friday, April 19,
a Watertown homeowner reported seeing blood

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:48.899
on the side of a boat in his yard.

00:15:48.899 --> 00:15:50.839
A SWAT team rushed to the home.

00:15:50.839 --> 00:15:53.350
Jahar had been hiding in the covered boat
for hours.

00:15:53.350 --> 00:15:55.709
The officers tempted to coax Jahar to come
out with tear gas.

00:15:55.709 --> 00:15:58.819
When that failed they fired bullets to scare
him out.

00:15:58.819 --> 00:16:01.999
In the end an imposing officer approached
the boat and loudly demanded that Jahar come

00:16:01.999 --> 00:16:02.999
out immediately.

00:16:02.999 --> 00:16:06.160
A childish voice replied . . .
But it’s going to hurt!

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:09.749
Police officers then moved in and helped Jahar
make his way down from the boat.

00:16:09.749 --> 00:16:14.100
He was severely wounded, with either bullet
or shrapnel injuries to the neck, ear and

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:15.100
thigh.

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:16.920
He was rushed to hospital where he was operated
on.

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:21.810
According to one of his nurses, he cried for
two days straight after his operation.

00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:25.019
When the police searched the inside of the
boat that had been Jahar’s final hideout,

00:16:25.019 --> 00:16:27.240
the found the following message written in
blood . . .

00:16:27.240 --> 00:16:31.749
The bombings were in retribution for the U.S.
crimes in places like Iraq and Afghanistan

00:16:31.749 --> 00:16:35.739
that the victims of the Boston bombing were
collateral damage in the same way innocent

00:16:35.739 --> 00:16:39.680
victims have been collateral damage in U.S.
wars around the world.

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:42.049
Jahar’s trial began on January 5, 2015.

00:16:42.049 --> 00:16:46.489
He was charged with four counts of murder,
along with 26 other charges.

00:16:46.489 --> 00:16:48.839
The prosecution sought the death penalty.

00:16:48.839 --> 00:16:53.230
Even though Massachusetts had outlawed the
death penalty in 1988, the federal charges

00:16:53.230 --> 00:16:54.230
against Tsarnaev made him eligible for execution.

00:16:54.230 --> 00:16:56.119
He plead not guilty to all of the charges.

00:16:56.119 --> 00:16:59.600
The defense position was that Tamerlan had
been the mastermind of the enterprise and

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:02.249
that Jahar had been coerced into cooperating.

00:17:02.249 --> 00:17:07.039
Tsarnaev showed no emotion throughout the
trial until his family members took the stand.

00:17:07.039 --> 00:17:09.339
At that point he wept bitterly.

00:17:09.339 --> 00:17:13.350
On April 8, 2015, Jahar was found guilty on
all 30 charges.

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:16.029
A month later he was sentenced to death by
lethal injection.

00:17:16.029 --> 00:17:20.919
Dzhokhar Tsarnaev now sits in the notorious
supermax prison ADX Florence in Fremont County,

00:17:20.919 --> 00:17:21.919
Colorado.

00:17:21.919 --> 00:17:40.830
Meanwhile his defense team are working on
an appeal to his death sentence.

